I walk out of the fitting room with the blue shirt.
The bigger size fits perfectly.
The clerk is still standing at the register.
"Is it better?" she asks with a smile.
"Yes, it is much better," I answer.
"The smaller shirt was too tight," I explain.
"I would like to exchange for this one."
"That is completely fine," she says.
"May I see your receipt again?" she asks.
I give her the small paper receipt.
She scans the barcode.
"There, now it is exchanged," she says.
"It does not cost extra."
"Thank you very much for the help," I say.
"You are welcome, and have a good day," she answers.
I put the shirt down into my bag.
Now I finally have some good clothes for the spring.
I walk out of the store.
I am very satisfied as I walk home.
